<title>UK: UK election-Conservatives 143; Labour 411-0413 GMT.</title>
<headline>UK election-Conservatives 143; Labour 411-0413 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of the number of parliamentary seats each party has won so far in Britain's election, the share of votes each has polled, and the estimated final tally of seats for each party, with 604 results in from Britain's 659 constituencies -</p>
<p>CONSERVATIVES.......143 (143 held, 171 lost)</p>
<p>LABOUR..............411 (269 held, 142 gained)</p>
<p>LIBERAL DEMOCRATS....39 (12 held, 27 gained, 2 lost)</p>
<p>OTHERS...............11 (7 held, 4 gained)</p>
<p>Average swing to Labour from Conservatives - 10.3 percent</p>
<p>Projected final total of seats according to BBC estimate -</p>
<p>CONSERVATIVES.......163</p>
<p>LABOUR..............421</p>
<p>LIBERAL DEMOCRATS....46</p>
<p>OTHERS...............29</p>
<p>Predicted majority for Labour - 183</p>
<p>Share of the vote so far - Conservatives 31 percent, Labour 45 percent, Liberal Democrats 17 percent</p>
</text>
